    { t: "open", q: "Why does the poet repeat the last line, 'And miles to go before I sleep'? Answer in two or three sentences.", m: "The poet repeats the line to stress that the speaker still has a long way to travel and many promises to keep before he can rest. The repetition shows his determination, and it also gives the poem a slow, calm ending like a lullaby. The second 'sleep' may also suggest the final rest at the end of life.", x: "اذكر في إجابتك: (1) المعنى الحرفي: طريق طويل، (2) المعنى الأعمق: واجبات الحياة، (3) أثر التكرار: التأكيد والعزم ونهاية هادئة." }
